alias ExitStatus = std::process::ExitStatus;
alias Inputs = std::process::Inputs;

public fn run(inputs: Inputs) -> status: ExitStatus pure waits doc "The css_selectors_oracle entry, invoked as `css_selectors_oracle CONTENT CASES` with both paths relative to the working directory, as tests/css/selectors_oracle.py runs it. CONTENT is WPT's ParentNode-querySelector-All-content.html. It is parsed by parse_document with scripting off, into an atom table that every case then shares. Then it emulates WPT's setupSpecialElements on the first element in tree order whose id attribute is `root`, with the part of it that pkg::dom can represent: it appends the HTML elements `null` and `undefined`, then a div with id `any-namespace` holding the divs `any-namespace-div1` and `any-namespace-div2`, then a div with id `no-namespace` holding `no-namespace-div1` and `no-namespace-div2`, every one an HTML element, as the harness's createElement and createElementNS with the XHTML namespace make them. The harness's third and fourth divs of each group, in no namespace and in http://www.example.org/ns, and the title attribute in that namespace that it adds to #attr-presence-i1 are not representable and are left out; the oracle excludes the cases that need them. The id-less divs that the harness's static NodeList checks append are not part of the document the oracle defines. The match context's target is the first element in tree order whose id attribute is `target`, or None when there is none, and its scope is None. CASES is the case file the oracle writes: per case, a line holding KIND and the input's byte length in decimal separated by one space, the input's bytes and a line feed. Every input is tokenized by parse_component_values and passed as the range over the whole component list. For KIND 0 it prints parse_an_plus_b's result as `[A, B]` with JSON integers, or `null`. For KIND 1 it prints `null` when parse_selector_list returns Invalid and `\"driver: too large\"` when it returns TooLarge; otherwise it calls selector_matches on every Element node of the document in tree order, descending into children and not into template contents, and prints the JSON array of the values of the id attributes of the elements that match, each escaped as a JSON string, with `\"driver: element without id\"` in place of a matching element that has no id attribute. An input that parse_component_values refuses prints `\"driver: tokenizer refused\"`, one longer than it admits `\"driver: case too large\"`, and one whose component list passes a ComponentRange's reach `\"driver: component list too long\"`. It exits with 0 after printing every case, and with 2 and a message on standard error, after the lines of the cases before it, when it is not given exactly two arguments, a file cannot be read, the document cannot be built as described, or the case file is malformed, including a KIND other than 0 and 1.";
